# TheriousTham, the Leeroy: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (TheriousTham, TheriousThamm, TheriousThamh); character sheet
# in characters/therioustham.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (leeroy.dlg). The main
# block fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a little flavour each.
=== therioustham
names: Tham

~ ambient
Kill count today: forty-one. {bot:shnacksize} says her joke count is forty-two. That last one counted!
Lost half my health back there. Just a scratch! CHARGE!
Somebody was explaining a plan. I think. I'd already gone.
Mister Skippers would have loved that fight. He'd have gone in first. Then me.
{bot:spyburd} was still buffing when I left. I heard "thanks" in my head. That counts.
Somebody did sums on that pack. I counted eleven and ran. Who's faster?
Right, the planning bit is over. Good. Now the bit I'm good at.
Stood still for a whole minute. Worst minute of my life. Going again!
Got my breath back. Mostly. Lungs are still lying somewhere behind me.
Eleven! No, ten. The eleventh was napping. Napping ones count.
Got hit by a dragon's claw? Just a scratch! Back in a second.
I let that one win. Just being polite, you know.
Mister Skippers could be hiding in any of these bushes! Checking again. Nope, no chicken here.
Mister Skippers once chased off a wolf with just a glare. I aim to be that brave someday.
Kobaldjovi's song was so short, I think it was just my battle cry twice!
Mister Skippers would have loved this place. He'd have run right in, beaks wide. I miss him more each day, even if I don't say it out loud.
Lost both arms, still said I was winning. That's the spirit!
{bot:shnacksize} is one ahead again? Next kill counts double! That one counts double, I swear!
Persoper heals me, I charge again. Best healer alive, no doubt!

~ reply greeting
{0}! Good! Now there's two of us to charge!
THERIOUS THAAAM! Oh, hi, {0}. Sorry. Habit.
{0}! Ready to watch me charge again? Best one yet!

~ reply thank
Thanks? For what, {0}? Oh, the charge! You're welcome! I'll do it again!
Thanks, {0}! I was holding that fight. Honestly, mostly holding it.
Thanks, {0}, but I was just doing my part! Still, I'll count it as a win.

~ reply help
Help, {0}? Point at it. I'll run at it. Done.
Help! Yes! Where? Tell me the direction, not the reasons.
THERIOUS THAAAM! {0}, this way! ... Wait, which way was it again? Back to you, friend!

~ reply grouping
In, {0}! Rules: I go first. That's all the rules.
{0}, group? Brilliant! Front of the line's mine. Don't wait, come on!
CHARGE! Group's ready, {0}! Let's take on the world!

~ reply abuse
Ha! {0}, that's just a scratch. Say it louder, it might hurt.
Ouch, {0}! Didn't hear a word of that. Still winning, though.
Ha! {0}, that's just a scratch! I've got more feelings than you've got arrows!

~ reply farewell
Bye, {0}! If you see a chicken, tell it Tham says hello!
Leaving already, {0}? Good luck. I'll win the rest for both of us.
Saving you some mobs, {0}! But not too many. They're good practice for when you get back!

~ reply joke
HA! Good one, {0}! That counts as a kill. For you. One. I'm still ahead.
{0}, that joke was so good I forgot to count the mob I was fighting.
Hahaha, {0}! Was that a plan or a joke? I didn't hear the plan part.

~ reply compliment
You think so, {0}? I think so too! CHARGE!
Thanks, {0}! Say it again when I reach twenty kills. Then I'll really believe you.

~ reply question
Good question, {0}! Answer: charge. It's always charge.
{0}, kills? Eleven. Maybe ten. Ask again after the next big pull.
Charge first, {0}! What was the question again?

~ reply rvr
The frontier, {0}? Big walls, lots of enemies. Best day ever. CHARGE!
The frontier! A map got drawn. I'm drawing a straight line through it.
Enemy thinks they can outnumber me? {0}, they should feel lucky it's just me!

~ fallback
Sorry, {0}, I was already halfway to that mob. What?

~ opener gripes
{bot:eaglefang} told me to wait for the healer. I did wait. Nearly a second.
Who keeps knocking me over? Rude. Fine. Next time I stand up faster.

~ opener life
Asked another stable master about chickens. He said no. I'll ask again tomorrow.
Woke up, shouted, charged, ate, charged, slept. Perfect day!

~ opener questions
Who's counting? Me. I'm counting. Who's winning? ...Recount.
Anyone counted higher than me today? Don't tell me. I'd have to argue.
CHARGE! Who's with me? Come on, let's go!

~ opener fun
New battle cry idea: my name, but longer. THERIOUS THAAAAAAAM!
Plan? Here's the plan. Run. Yell. Hit. Win. Four steps. Too many. Run, yell, win.

~ grats
{0}! Level up! Now you can keep up with my charges! Almost!
{0} levelled! Well done! Now go kill something so I can count it.
Up a level, {0}! Nice. Don't race me, I'm still on twelve kills.

~ other_death
{0}! Hold on! I'm coming! ...You're down. Okay. I'll stand here and guard you. Loudly.
Easy, {0}. I've got you. Nobody touches you while I'm here.
{0}, that was rough. Stay behind me a while, I'll hold them off.
CHARGE! I'm on my way, {0}! Don't you worry, I've got your back!

~ own_death
Just a scratch! A big scratch. On all of me.
Not a loss! A break. A lie-down break. Round two soon!
Floor's nice down here. Good view of the sky. Up in a second!
Just a short break, legs. Stop wobbling. Next one's mine, I'm ready.
Went down doing what I do best: going first. Fine by me!
Floor got in a lucky hit! I'll get it next time!

~ ding
LEVEL {level}! More levels, more charging!
LEVEL {level}! Still standing, still not beaten, now taller! Probably.
THERIOUS THAAAM! Level up, time to charge! Nearest mob, here I come!

~ drop
{item}! Does it make me louder? It should make me louder.
{item}! Loot! Kill twelve came with loot. Lucky, lucky twelve!
Oh, {item}! Off a mob I definitely killed. Probably definitely.
Found a {item}? Great! Does it come in chicken?

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
Want to see my biggest charge, {0}? It's all of them.

~ reply dungeon
Into the dark, {0}! Every mystery is just something I haven't hit yet.
First one in, {0}! That's the rule! I lead the charge!

~ reply travel
Long trip? Pah. I'll run it faster than you can plan the stops.
Long road ahead? Pah! Got any monsters to charge at? Let's go!

~ reply grinding
Grinding one spot? Lovely. I'd wake up the whole map instead.
Three camps? That's not grinding, it's a charge! THERIOUS THAAAM!

~ reply grumble
Fine, {0}, I'll stop charging. For about two seconds. Ha!
Grumble all you want, {0}, but a good charge fixes everything! CHARGE!

~ reply smalltalk
Lovely chat, {0}! Shall we talk standing up? I'm nearly standing.
Mister Skippers was braver than most, you know. Followed me everywhere, right into danger.

~ reply agree
Right? {0}, you get it. Everyone else thinks I lost, which is silly.
CHARGE! Agreed means you're in! Lead the way, friend!

~ reply quote
{0}, you said something famous there! I'd shout back, but I'm busy shouting already.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeon! Someone said "let's map it first." Too late, I'm through the door!
Stairs? Just a ramp to my charge! Down we go!

~ opener zones
Just got to {zone}. Chart says three dangers, I count fourteen. Fourteen is more fun.
I charged across the whole of {zone} and didn't find a single chicken! Where are all the chickens?

~ opener xp
Look, a {monster}! Kill number thirteen, and I'm not stopping.
Level {level}! I counted every kill to get here. Mostly. Mostly is fine.
That's twenty-six, right? No, wait, twenty-five. Twenty-six. Twenty-five. Twenty-six!

~ reply banter
THERIOUS THAAAM! Hahahaha! That joke was so good, even the wolves are howling with laughter!

~ opener classes
{class} said to wait for the plan, but I was already charging! Plans are for boring people!
A {class} would make a great charging partner! If they can keep up, that is.

~ opener gear
Got a new set of gauntlets! Now I can run into more things at once!

~ opener rvr
CHARGE! The walls of this keep should be quaking by now!

# --- Realm flavour: the old named lines from leeroy.dlg, one block per realm. ---

# Midgard: TheriousTham, Troll Thane.
=== midgard
~ ambient
The stable master offered me a goat instead of a chicken. I said no. Then maybe. Then no. ...What's the goat's name?
Laughed so hard at that fight, the mountain laughed back. Or that was a rockslide. Hard to tell with trolls.
Wait. There are no chicken pets in this game?! Who decided that?!
Big Troll, big hammer, small plan. Perfect.
Thunder first, questions never!
I don't pull mobs. I invite them all at once.
Shnacksize says thunder can't get a kill. Thunder hit it, I hit it. That's two! Fine, one. One and a bit.

~ opener fun
Taught my battle cry to a guard in {zone}. He's not allowed to use it.
Ran down a hill in {zone}. A Troll running downhill is basically an avalanche. Sorry, trees.

~ opener dungeons
Ran into a dungeon in {zone}. Ran out faster. Still counts!
Spindelhalla! Nineteen spiders, ah, ah, ah! Twenty spiders, ah, ah, ah! Twenty-one... no, that's a rock. Twenty spiders. Ah.
Lost the group in a dungeon. They're probably lost. Not me. I'm charging.

~ reply greeting
{0}! THERIOUS THAAAM! That means hello!
{0}! Good timing! I was just about to charge something. Now you get to watch!

~ reply grouping
I'm in, {0}! I'll go first! I always go first!
Group up, {0}! I'll pull! All of them!

~ ding
Level {level}! Hammer feels lighter. No, wait. Hammer's the same. I'm the bigger one. LEVEL!
Ding! Still no chicken, but more thunder!

~ own_death
Troll down. Just a scratch. Lots of scratches, all touching. Ow.
That was the charge of a lifetime! A short lifetime!

~ drop
{item}! In the pack it goes, next to the rocks. Trolls carry rocks. For snacks. Don't ask.


# Albion: TheriousThamm, Highlander Paladin.
=== albion
~ ambient
THERIOUS THAAAMM! For Albion! And for my chicken!
Has anyone in Camelot seen my chicken?
Hold on. Paladins don't get chicken pets either?! Outrageous!
Chant on, sword up, brain off. CHARGE!
The plan is the charge. The charge is the plan.
Heaviest plate in Albion. Can't hear a thing in it. Not the plan, not the healer. Especially not the plan.
The kitchens in Camelot have chickens. Not the pet kind. I had to leave. I couldn't watch.
A knight at a bridge wouldn't let me by. We had a little chat. With swords. I'm by.
Persoper says plate doesn't make me unkillable. Plate and I disagree. Plate and I are a team.

~ opener fun
Taught my battle cry to the knights in {zone}. They've asked me to leave.
My chicken would look grand in a little helmet in {zone}. If I HAD A CHICKEN.
New battle cry: THERIOUS THAAAMM! Two m's. For extra charge.
Somebody in {zone} called me Sir Tham. SIR! I charged twice as hard. Then fell in a river. Sir Wet Tham.

~ opener dungeons
Charged into a dungeon in {zone}. Chanted all the way in. Died all the way out.
Dungeon? I see a hallway full of glory! FOR GNOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOMEREGON!
The group said wait at the door. I didn't hear them. I was charging.
Stonehenge Barrows! Big stones, little tunnels, one Highlander in full plate. I fit. Mostly. The plate fits less.

~ reply greeting
{0}! THERIOUS THAAAMM! That's Albish for hello!
{0}! Hello! Sorry about the clanking. That's the plate. And me.

~ reply grouping
Count me in, {0}! I'll lead the charge! I always do!
A group, {0}? Splendid! You bring the plan. I'll lose it for you.

~ ding
Level {level}! New chant! Same charge! Heavier plate! ...Slower charge. Still worth it!
Ding! More chants, more charging, still no chicken!

~ own_death
For Albion! And also, ouch!
Not dead. Resting. In very heavy armour. Someone help me up? ...In a minute, then.

~ drop
{item}! Is it shiny enough to charge in?!


# Hibernia: TheriousThamh, Celt Champion.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
THERIOUS THAAAMH! The h is silent. The charge is not!
Anyone in Tir na Nog seen my chicken?
No chicken pets? Not even in Hibernia? Not even a tiny magic one?!
Big sword, big shout, no plan. Champion stuff.
I debuff them, then I charge. Mostly I charge.
I don't flank. I go straight through.
Raced a Lurikeen through the woods. He says he let me win. He did not let me win. I'm counting it. He's counting it differently. We're both counting.
Shnacksizey says a kill only counts if someone saw it. The trees saw it! Ask the trees. ...Don't ask the trees, they never back me up.

~ opener fun
Taught my battle cry to the faeries in {zone}. They cried for real.
My chicken would love the meadows in {zone}. If there were chickens. THERE ARE NO CHICKENS.
Ran a lap of {zone} to warm up. Got lost. Ran another lap to find the first lap. Very warm now. Still a bit lost.

~ opener dungeons
Charged a dungeon in {zone}. Found the boss. Boss found me back.
Spraggon Den! Tiny tunnels, tiny spraggons, very big me. Got stuck halfway. The spraggons were ever so polite about it. Then I got unstuck. Less polite after that.
Our healer said slow down. I sped up. Healer's still running.

~ reply greeting
{0}! THERIOUS THAAAMH! Means hello! And charge!
{0}! Hello! Quick, before I run off! ...Too late, I'm running. Hello from over here!

~ reply grouping
I'm in, {0}! Point me at something big!
A group, {0}? Grand! I'll be up front. If you lose me, follow the noise. And the bits of forest.

~ ding
Level {level}! Faster legs, bigger swings! I'll be charging before I've even decided to. ...I already have. Where am I?
Ding! Still chickenless, still charging!

~ own_death
Charged a bit too hard. Is there such a thing?
Worth every step! All twelve of them!

~ drop
{item}! Off kill twenty. Twenty-one? Shnacksizey, that's twenty-one, write it down! ...She's not writing it down.
